 "generatorWeaknesses": [
  "Taught words must describe the goal: the first word of `teach` is checked against the goal, the schema wants a non-empty `teach` on every step, and a step with conditions must have one (everyConditionAppearsInTheKoreanClue indexes teach[0]). There is no concept for 표지판 (sign) and `hoe` lists only the iron hoe, so a wooden-hoe or sign step cannot teach its own noun; the trails use other first words.",
  "SMELT names the output item literally: baked_potato reads 구운 감자를 요리해요 (cooked twice). Only a concept that covers the output (고기 for cooked meat, 생선 for cooked fish) gives a natural 요리하다 sentence, and both are unknown words on day one, so the one SMELT step (root finale) has two unknown words.",
  "The HOLDING phrase of a clue names the item (참나무 보트를 들고) while the generated hint uses the concept word (배를 들고): clue and hint disagree.",
  "NEAR_BLOCK is true only while the player looks at that block, so WAIT with NEAR_BLOCK (plant_seed, silk_touch_nest) asks the player to stare at the crop or the nest while waiting.",
  "coverage.py cuts 팔아요 into 파다 (a different verb), so 팔다 is never counted and every sell sentence carries a phantom unknown word.",
  "BREED with count 1 prints no counter (소를 키워요); a count above 1 adds the counter 마리, an extra unknown word. The three BREED finales use count 1.",
  "A step that names a biome by concept (바다, 강) needs the concept's tag (#minecraft:is_ocean, #minecraft:is_river); minecraft:ocean or minecraft:river fails the 'describes the goal' check, and the tags repeat existing REACH_BIOME signatures unless a condition is added.",
  "An authored clue must keep verb and object together (줘요 right after 건초 더미를): inserting a counter (한 개) between them fails 'clue does not name the action'. An authored hint must contain every taught noun (multiWordHintsExplainTheExtraNouns).",
  "The simulator counts every `teach` entry as an encounter even when the word is not in the sentence; this is the only way to bring a word to three encounters when a trail has fewer than three sentences that can carry it.",
  "On a fresh worktree gates.sh fails at the coverage step until a full `./gradlew test` has written build/reports/content/verb-forms.json.",
  "ObtainabilityTest.everyGoalTargetIsARealVanillaId had no case for BREED and MOUNT (cow, horse, bee looked up as blocks), and PlaytestTest fed only one animal for BREED, which wave 4 no longer accepts: the first trails to use these goals had to fix both tests.",
  "USE_BLOCK on a sign has no verb: the default was 쓰다 (use/write/wear), now 사용하다; make_a_sign_glow uses an authored clue (표지판에 글을 써요)."
 ]
